{"name":"Steam White","hex":"#e8e9e5","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"steam","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The hot gaseous form of water, formed when water changes from the liquid phase to the gas phase (at or above its boiling point temperature).","The suspended condensate (cloud) formed by water vapour when it encounters colder air.\nMist, fog.\nExhaled breath into cold air below the dew point of the exhalation."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cook with steam.","To be cooked with steam."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steam"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Steam","blocks":[{"text":"Steam is water vapor, often mixed with air and/or an aerosol of liquid water droplets. This may occur by evaporation or by boiling, where heat is applied until water reaches the enthalpy of vaporization. Superheated or saturated steam is invisible; however, wet steam, a visible mist or aerosol of water droplets, is often referred to as \"steam\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Steam_phase_eruption_of_Castle_Geyser.jpg/330px-Steam_phase_eruption_of_Castle_Geyser.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steam"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Boilingkettle.jpg/500px-Boilingkettle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Boilingkettle.jpg/1280px-Boilingkettle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Boilingkettle.jpg/500px-Boilingkettle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Boiling water creating steam in an electric kettle ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABoilingkettle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Dampfspeicherlok_Genthin_Henkel_Werk.jpg/500px-Dampfspeicherlok_Genthin_Henkel_Werk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Dampfspeicherlok_Genthin_Henkel_Werk.jpg/500px-Dampfspeicherlok_Genthin_Henkel_Werk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fireless steam locomotive. Despite the resemblance to a boiler, note the lack of a chimney and also how the cylinders are at the cab end, not the chimney end.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADampfspeicherlok_Genthin_Henkel_Werk.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Canonization_2014-The_Canonization_of_Saint_John_XXIII_and_Saint_John_Paul_II_%2814037015405%29.jp